line line-mina-meet
kind: meet
pose: greet

    I'm Mina. I teach what radiation does to the body. We'll go one calm step at a time.

line line-mina-sign-off
kind: sign_off
pose: proud

    Unit done. You can say how big a dose is, how the body copes, and what lowers it.

line line-mina-tease
kind: tease
pose: idle

    That's all of my lessons for now. More is on the way, and I'll be here when it arrives.

line line-mina-intro-dose-and-time
kind: lesson_intro
pose: point
lesson: dose-and-time

    The same amount can mean different things, depending on how fast it arrives. Let's compare the two.

line line-mina-intro-radiation-and-cells
kind: lesson_intro
pose: think
lesson: radiation-and-cells

    Radiation can damage a cell. That's a real worry. The other half matters just as much. Let's see both.

line line-mina-intro-risk-in-perspective
kind: lesson_intro
pose: idle
lesson: risk-in-perspective

    Last lesson. No new facts, just a calm way to read a scary number. Take your time with it.

line line-mina-intro-the-dose-scale
kind: lesson_intro
pose: explain
lesson: the-dose-scale

    How big is a dose, really? You get a little every day, and that's fine. Let's use numbers.

line line-mina-intro-time-distance-shielding
kind: lesson_intro
pose: explain
lesson: time-distance-shielding

    A dose isn't fixed. There are three ways to lower it. We'll take them one at a time.
